    "status": "present",
    "value": "Maximize a building height with nonnegative heights, building1 fixed at zero, adjacent differences at most one, and supplied upper restrictions. The approach is: two directional Lipschitz caps, then interval tent maxima and unrestricted tail. Its target cost is O(r log r) time/O(r) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
